/// Complete 1:1 port of `Tests/IOSKeyboardTests.swift` (1,393 lines) covering:
/// 1–4. iOS 26 440pt Pro Max 32-key grid, Voronoi hit-testing, Shift/CapsLock, `123`/`#+=` planes
/// 5. `SpaceTrackpadAccumulator` + velocity boost + `IOSTextCursorNavigation`
/// 6–10. End-to-end `JuxuSession` view-space touch slip rescue, `ergonomicThumbYBias`, dynamic `validNextMask`,
///       top-edge Spacebar protection, Sacred Keycap Core (`3.0pt x 2.6pt`), 220pt portrait & 903pt transient clamp
/// 11, 13, 15. `IOSClipboardParser`, `IOSClipboardSuggestionStore` (2-step lookup & denied pasteboard), `IOSClipboardVisibilityGate`
/// 14. `WBAUX003` idle predictions & punctuation reset
/// 16. Neural `nextKeyPriors` (Key #1 & valid-vs-valid tie) + personal 52-float `touchOffsets` + `compensatedLetterPoint`
/// 17–19. Cangjie radicals, Wubi 86/98/06 radicals, T9 9-key Pinyin layout & T9 neural/personal priors
/// 20. `IOSSwipeUp`, `IOSKeyAlternates`, `IOSLineClear`, `IOSLineClearUndo`, `IOSBackspaceChunkDelete`, `cleanIOSCandidateAnnotation`
/// 21. `IOSInlineMarkedTextSession` (`YYTextViewDocumentMock` + `StandardUITextViewMock` + `TIKeyboardOutputProxyMock` + orphan sweep)
/// 22. `IOSKeyboardTrackpadHold` & `spaceCommaKeyEnabled` WeChat bottom row (`1.85 / 1.0 / 3.6 / 1.15 / 1.85` pitches, `usesFunctionFill`).

